    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332-a1">

                <pb facs="0596" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg502"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Marquis of Lansdowne to
                        Mr. Stanhope</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Government House, Ottawa</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 9, 1886</date>. (Received November
                    22.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Earl Granville’s dispatch
                    of the 24th June last, respecting the fisheries question and inclosing copies of
                    two letters from the foreign office and one from the United States minister in
                    London, addressed to the secretary of state <pb facs="0597" n="503"
                        xml:id="pg503"/> for foreign affairs, I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    a copy of an approved minute of the privy council of Canada concurring in a
                    report of the minister of justice dealing with the points raised by Mr. Phelps
                    in his note of the 2d June last on the subject of the seizure of the United
                    States fishing Vessel <hi rendition="#italic">David J. Adams</hi>, near Digby,
                    Nova Scotia.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansdowne.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
